  </section>

  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Exit Device Expertise</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Panic Bar Services We Provide</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          From new panic bar installation on existing doors to repair, replacement, and integration with master key systems, we provide complete exit device services for Delaware commercial properties.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">

        <!-- Card 1 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.42 15.17L17.25 21A2.652 2.652 0 0021 17.25l-5.877-5.877M11.42 15.17l2.496-3.03c.317-.384.74-.626 1.208-.766M11.42 15.17l-4.655 5.653a2.548 2.548 0 11-3.586-3.586l6.837-5.63m5.108-.233c.55-.164 1.163-.188 1.743-.14a4.5 4.5 0 004.486-6.336l-3.276 3.277a3.004 3.004 0 01-2.25-2.25l3.276-3.276a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.336 4.486c.091 1.076-.071 2.264-.904 2.95l-.102.085m-1.745 1.437L5.909 7.5H4.5L2.25 3.75l1.5-1.5L7.5 4.5v1.409l4.26 4.26m-1.745 1.437l1.745-1.437m6.615 8.206L15.75 15.75M4.867 19.125h.008v.008h-.008v-.008z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Rim Exit Device Installation</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Rim exit devices are the most common panic bar type — the mechanism mounts on the surface of the door and the bar engages a rim latch on the door edge. They are widely used because they are versatile, compatible with most hollow metal and wood door configurations, and relatively straightforward to install and service.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We install single-door and double-door rim exit device configurations, with or without exterior key cylinders. For exterior access, we fit a key cylinder into the outside trim so the door can be locked and unlocked from outside while always freely opening from inside by pushing the bar.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            Rim exit devices can be keyed to match your existing <a href="/services/commercial-lock-rekeying" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">commercial key system</a> or integrated into a new <a href="/services/master-key-systems" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key hierarchy</a> so one key operates all your building's locks.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 2 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 21h16.5M4.5 3h15M5.25 3v18m13.5-18v18M9 6.75h1.5m-1.5 3h1.5m-1.5 3h1.5m3-6H15m-1.5 3H15m-1.5 3H15M9 21v-3.375c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h3.75c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125V21" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Vertical Rod Exit Device Installation</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Vertical rod exit devices are used on double doors and doors where the bottom of the door must be secured in addition to the top. The panic bar connects to rods that extend vertically to strike points at the top and bottom of the door frame, providing a more secure latch than a rim device.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Surface vertical rod (SVR) devices mount the rods on the surface of the door, making them simpler to install on doors not prepped for concealed hardware. Concealed vertical rod (CVR) devices route the rods through the interior of the door for a cleaner appearance — suitable for storefront glass doors and aesthetic-sensitive applications.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            We advise on the appropriate device type based on your door construction, frame condition, and security requirements before any installation work begins.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 3 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9.594 3.94c.09-.542.56-.94 1.11-.94h2.593c.55 0 1.02.398 1.11.94l.213 1.281c.063.374.313.686.645.87.074.04.147.083.22.127.324.196.72.257 1.075.124l1.217-.456a1.125 1.125 0 011.37.49l1.296 2.247a1.125 1.125 0 01-.26 1.431l-1.003.827c-.293.24-.438.613-.431.992a6.759 6.759 0 010 .255c-.007.378.138.75.43.99l1.005.828c.424.35.534.954.26 1.43l-1.298 2.247a1.125 1.125 0 01-1.369.491l-1.217-.456c-.355-.133-.75-.072-1.076.124a6.57 6.57 0 01-.22.128c-.331.183-.581.495-.644.869l-.213 1.28c-.09.543-.56.941-1.11.941h-2.594c-.55 0-1.02-.398-1.11-.94l-.213-1.281c-.062-.374-.312-.686-.644-.87a6.52 6.52 0 01-.22-.127c-.325-.196-.72-.257-1.076-.124l-1.217.456a1.125 1.125 0 01-1.369-.49l-1.297-2.247a1.125 1.125 0 01.26-1.431l1.004-.827c.292-.24.437-.613.43-.992a6.932 6.932 0 010-.255c.007-.378-.138-.75-.43-.99l-1.004-.828a1.125 1.125 0 01-.26-1.43l1.297-2.247a1.125 1.125 0 011.37-.491l1.216.456c.356.133.751.072 1.076-.124.072-.044.146-.087.22-.128.332-.183.582-.495.644-.869l.214-1.281z" />
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Panic Bar Repair & Service</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Panic bars see heavy use in commercial settings — they are pushed hundreds of times a day in high-traffic facilities. Over time, internal mechanisms wear, latches fail to retract fully, bars become stiff, or the mounting hardware loosens. A panic bar that does not function reliably is both a code violation and a life safety issue.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We diagnose and repair panic bar failures on-site. Common issues include worn or broken latch mechanisms, failed spring return, misaligned strike plates, loose or damaged mounting arms, and corroded components. In many cases, targeted repair or parts replacement resolves the issue without full unit replacement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            When a panic bar is beyond economical repair, we supply and install a replacement unit matched to your door specifications, keyed to your existing system if applicable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 4 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v3.75m0-10.036A11.959 11.959 0 013.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 003 9.75c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.57-.598-3.75h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.249-8.25-3.286zm0 13.036h.008v.008H12v-.008z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Alarmed Exit Devices</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            For doors that should only be used as emergency exits — not as a general entry and exit point — alarmed exit devices add an audible alarm that triggers whenever the bar is pushed. This deters casual misuse of emergency exits while still allowing free egress in genuine emergencies.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Alarmed exit devices are common in retail environments to prevent shoplifting through back exits, in warehouses to control which doors are used for normal traffic, and in schools and facilities to limit unauthorized access. Most units include a delay feature that allows the alarm to be silenced with a code or key within a brief window.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            We install standalone alarmed exit devices as well as systems that integrate with your existing security infrastructure. Call us to discuss the right configuration for your specific property and traffic patterns.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 5 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.75 5.25a3 3 0 013 3m3 0a6 6 0 01-7.029 5.912c-.563-.097-1.159.026-1.563.43L10.5 17.25H8.25v2.25H6v2.25H2.25v-2.818c0-.597.237-1.17.659-1.591l6.499-6.499c.404-.404.527-1 .43-1.563A6 6 0 1121.75 8.25z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Panic Bar Keying & Master Key Integration</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Most panic bar exit devices allow a key cylinder to be installed in the exterior trim, enabling the door to be locked from the outside with a key. This is essential for exit-only doors that should not be accessible from outside without authorization — loading docks, fire exits used as secondary entry points, and back-of-house doors in retail environments.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We key panic bar cylinders to match your existing facility key system so that building managers do not need to carry a separate key. For properties with a formal <a href="/services/master-key-systems" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key system</a>, we integrate panic bar cylinders into the hierarchy at the appropriate level.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
